<TopicLayout slug="gospel">
  <p class="lede">
    The Gospel means good news, but in order to understand this good news we must first understand the bad news that currently is.
  </p>
  <p>
    <b>The bad news that is: </b>
    <br>
    You're as bad as bad can be. Period.
    <br />
    You may not know it, there's no way of you fixing it, no reason to deny it, and only one eternal outcome
    because of it - Hell.
  </p>
  <p>
    <b>The Good News: </b>
    <br>
    There is a good God who became a good man in order to empathize with the weakness of bad men. 
    <br>He died in a bad man's way,
    <br>went to hell and suffered a bad man's penalty, 
    <br>and was rasied to life to bring new life, eternal life, to bad men who believe that He has indeed done it.
  </p>
  <p>
    True faith in all this will transform the bad man into the image of the good man, which was a part
    of the good God's plan all along. 
  </p>
  <p><b>Do you believe it?</b></p>
